      "writtenOn": "2026-04-28T09:38:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Having only an API to set the surfaces is likely not enough, as the changes to the test code show: when handing a replay, the application using the replay can\u0027t know a priori how many surfaces are needed and of what size. In the tests we hardcode 1 surface but it\u0027s only because we have specific knowledge of the workload.\n\nInstead we could have a new API here that gives reflection of how many surfaces need to be provided, as well as some metadata about them, like their first configured size and label. This why users of the replay API can size the windows and set their title to match.\n\nThen the changes in DawnTest.h/.cpp and SurfaceTests.cpp can be changed to automatically spawn GLFW windows as needed when starting to run the replay. Likewise in CaptureAndReaplayTests.cpp.",
      "revId": "e6936e31b731c89565c1f0183f22b0ab16294f03",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
